        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2003 SANFL Grand Final\n- Organizations: West Adelaide Football Club, South Australian National Football League\n- Places: Richmond Oval, City Mazda Stadium\n- Concepts: Australian rules football\n\nFacts:\n- The 2003 South Australian National Football League Grand Final ended with the Central District Bulldogs defeating West Adelaide by 34 points to win the club's third premiership.\n- West Adelaide Football Club is an Australian rules football club in the South Australian National Football League.\n- West Adelaide Football Club is commonly known as The Bloods and Westies.\n- West Adelaide Football Club's home base is Richmond Oval, which is currently known as City Mazda Stadium under a sponsorship agreement.",
